/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  MEASURED vapour-liquid equilibrium of nitrogen (1) + methane (2) at 149.82 K
  (-190.00 degF), seven rows -- the fit case's evidence.

  SOURCE (the page, read from the page image): Stryjek, R.; Chappelear, P.S.;
  Kobayashi, R.  "Low-Temperature Vapor-Liquid Equilibria of Nitrogen-Methane
  System", J. Chem. Eng. Data 19 (1974) 334-339, Table III, the isotherm
  "T = -190.00 F = -123.33 C = 149.82 K", p. 338 (page 5 of the PDF).  Columns
  as printed: P in psia, nitrogen mole fraction in the liquid and in the vapour.
  alpha = K_N2/K_CH4 = (y/x)/((1-y)/(1-x)) is computed from those two columns.

  NOT USED, with the reason: the pure-methane row (149.5 psia, the vapour
  pressure, K_N2 extrapolated, footnote b); the 300 psia row (liquid
  composition not determined); the 664 psia critical point (x = y = 0.6528);
  and the 649 psia row (x 0.5866), 2.3 % of the critical pressure below the
  critical point, where a cubic has no bubble point worth fitting (the rule is
  declared in the README: rows within 3 % of the isotherm's critical pressure
  are discarded BEFORE the fit).
  Rows 1, 3, 5, 7 are the FIT; rows 2, 4, 6 (202.5, 299, 495 psia) are HELD OUT.
  Row 4 (299 psia, x 0.1503, y 0.4579, K_N2 3.047) is the anchor of
  tutorials/steady/flash/flash09_n2ch4_stryjek.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     binaryVLE.P_bubble;
system       ( N2 CH4 );

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus transcribedNotCheckedAgainstArticle;
    citation     "Stryjek, R.; Chappelear, P.S.; Kobayashi, R. (1974). Low-temperature vapor-liquid equilibria of nitrogen-methane system. J. Chem. Eng. Data 19, 334-339, Table III (p. 338), isotherm 149.82 K. doi:10.1021/je60063a023";
    sourceFile   "stryjek1974-nitrogen-methane-vle-low-temperature.pdf";
    sha256       "e02c272d31586c6280f9f6c341ff222779f2b830e78bef81806260d9d1c35b1b";   // of that PDF
}

columns
(
    { name x[N2];  unit -;  }
    { name T;  unit K;  }
    { name P_bubble;  unit psi;  }
    { name y_eqT_N2;  unit -;  }
    { name alpha;  unit -;  }
);

data
(
    0.02838  149.82   179.0  0.1529  6.1796
    0.05140  149.82   202.5  0.2404  5.8408
    0.09849  149.82   249.5  0.3683  5.3367
    0.15030  149.82   299.0  0.4579  4.7753
    0.25790  149.82   396.5  0.5779  3.9396
    0.37780  149.82   495.0  0.6480  3.0318
    0.50340  149.82   594.0  0.6867  2.1622
);
